# Lovable Project Workflow

This project is managed by **Lovable** (lovable.dev). All code changes must respect Lovable's conventions and sync model.

## Core Principles

- Lovable is the source of truth for the UI and component structure. Do not restructure, rename, or reorganize files/folders that Lovable manages unless explicitly asked.
- Never delete or modify files under `src/integrations/lovable/` — these are auto-generated by Lovable.
- Keep the `src/components/ui/` directory aligned with shadcn/ui conventions. Lovable generates these; only extend, never replace.
- Supabase edge functions live in `supabase/functions/`. Follow the existing pattern when adding new ones.

## Git Workflow

- All changes made locally (via Cursor) must be committed and pushed to `origin/main` so Lovable can pick them up.
- Before starting work, always pull latest from `origin/main` — Lovable may have pushed changes.
- Use the `sync_repo.py` script for automated 2-way sync between local and Lovable/GitHub.
- Write clear, atomic commit messages. Lovable reads commit history.

## Code Conventions

- Use TypeScript strict patterns (the project uses `@/*` path aliases mapped to `src/*`).
- Styling: Tailwind CSS utility classes. The project uses a custom glassmorphic design system defined in `tailwind.config.ts`.
- State: React Query for server state, React context for auth. Do not introduce Redux or Zustand.
- Components: Functional React components only. Use shadcn/ui primitives from `src/components/ui/`.
- Environment variables go in `.env` (never commit secrets). Supabase keys are configured via `src/integrations/supabase/client.ts`.

## What NOT to Change Without Explicit Request

- `components.json` (shadcn/ui config)
- `src/integrations/` (auto-generated)
- `vite.config.ts` (Lovable plugin config)
- `.lovable/` directory
